      "id": "1aff90f862d58cee350b3da184541ac9bb8fa991",
      "message": "[ota-hal] OTA-1690: the cap speaks\n\nStep-4 mundane reader (narrative-agency audit, hole 9): the two lifetime\nstanding budgets stopped the number in silence. Gifts to a faction's\npeople are capped at GIFT_STANDING_FACTION_CAP per faction and the\nrivals' gratitude for spiting someone else at SPITE_STANDING_FACTION_CAP\n\u2014 both by design, both asymmetric (losses stay uncapped) \u2014 but once a\nbudget was spent the standing line simply never printed again, which\nreads as a broken counter rather than a rule.\n\nOne line at the CROSSING, and never again after it (factions\n.standingCapLine, called from both writers in gameStore):\n\n- gift: \"<Faction> has taken your measure through gifts already \u2014 from\n  here on a present wins the person, not the banner.\" (the gift still\n  lands on the person's ledger, as before)\n- spite: \"Their rivals' gratitude has a ceiling \u2014 <Faction> will not\n  think better of you for spiting someone else again.\"\n\nSuite: __tests__/ota1690TheCapSpeaks.test.ts (the crossing fires once,\nunder-cap and already-capped gains are silent, both sites wired).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LGFtzR6AQJbu4XdR28y3fX",
